; divfull-fp64.cfta - the WHOLE divide on the chip, fp64
;
; python/cft_golden/divfull.py's div_full_program(fp64) as a file:
; the operands raw in r0 and r1, the class read off the encoding, the
; specials answered by SELECT in softfloat.div's order, subnormals
; scaled by 2^p, the core (seed, 3 Newton steps, the truncating
; Markstein finish, two restore passes) on the centred operands, then
; round_pack in integer instructions - the normal path packing with
; the carry riding into the exponent field, the subnormal path's kept
; being the fraction field, tininess after rounding. Two deposits a
; lane: the correctly rounded quotient and its five IEEE flags.
;
; BANK_EXT: the run supplies 42 constants - divfull.bank(fp64, rnd) -
; the last five of which are the rounding mode as 0/1 words (RNE, RTZ,
; RDN, RUP, RMM), so one image serves every attribute. Nothing per
; element is computed on the host; libcft copies deposit 0 and ORs
; deposit 1 (host/src/divsqrt.c, the whole-program route, from the
; generated host/src/divfull_images.h).
;
; The check is byte equality with the image the model generates, and
; the run arm holds the deposits to softfloat.div, specials included.
;
;   r0  a, raw     r1  b, raw
;   deposits: quotient, flags

.format   fp64
.deposits 2
.bank     external
